  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Cooler and drier conditions are forecast for Saturday, \nbefore showers and thunderstorms return Sunday.\n\nSurface ridging builds in for Saturday supporting fair weather \nconditions. Warm air and moisture advection atop a shallow cool \nlayer will support scattered showers across the northern half of\nthe fcst area late Sat night into Sunday. Then, additional \nshowers and thunderstorms are expected Sunday afternoon and \nevening along a retreating warm front. The front will sink south\nSunday night as low pressure passes by and high pressure starts\nbuilding south again. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Daily chances for showers persists into next week \nalong with cooler temperatures. \n\nUpper-level ridging breaks down early next week, with multiple \nshortwave disurbances moving across the Mid-Atlantic in the days \nfollowing. Mid-level moisture brought in from the south will \ncontinue overhead as winds flow northeasterly. As a result, daily \nshowers remain a possibility into late next week as these \ndisturbances slowly track across the region. Temperatures drop \non Tuesday in the wake of one of these disturbances, with highs \ngenerally ranging in the upper 50s and 60s. This cooler- than- \naverage weather persists at least through midweek as nearby \ndisturbances continue to bring rain showers to the area. Towards\nthe bay & coastlines, wind gusts could remain elevated mid-to- \nlate week as these disturbances begin to track offshore. \nOverall, coastal flooding could become something to watch out \nfor next week as these elevated winds combined with persistent \nrain stretches on.",
